# sgo.build (schema: see the sgola tree's core/sgo.build). wata-ios is an APP
# over core + json + wataclient + wataui: the iOS client (plan 0044),
# wata-mac's architecture with UIKit under it — wata-fb's screen bodies
# (copied in, honest duplication) on the retained UIKit stage, the audio
# thread stubbed off, key input as the shell's touch keypad.
mode app
emitname wata-ios
binname wata-ios
gomod wataios
optreport
# The UIKit shell and glue: iosshell owns UIApplicationMain, the delegate,
# the window and the ready hop; iosui owns the main-queue seam, the pool
# brackets, the cast facets, the raw-RGBA crossing and the render probe. They
# ride appleptt (the generated uikit bindings), which needs its OWN godep
# line — a `replace` in a dependency's go.mod is ignored by Go once the
# emitted app is the main module, so each local sibling must be replaced from
# the app's go.mod, and a godep line is exactly that (require + local
# replace).
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/iosshell go-pkgs/iosshell
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/iosui go-pkgs/iosui
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/appleptt go-pkgs/appleptt
# the timeout-carrying http.Client constructor (plan 0045 slice 1) — the
# net/http facade binds the Client type, not its fields, so the per-request
# Timeout comes from this tiny Go package, same as wata-fb and wata-mac
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/httpc go-pkgs/httpc
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/irohnet go-pkgs/irohnet
